Total budget exceeded by 45 due to marker appended after truncation. Need ensure total ≤ limit. In finalize:

```rust
if text.len() > remaining {
   text = take(remaining)
   marker...
   if text+marker <= limit { push marker } // this checks against global limit, not remaining; remaining = limit - used, so text+marker <= limit allows overflow by used.
}
```
Should check `text.len() + marker.len() <= remaining` OR truncate further to fit marker. Simplest: if remaining == 0 → text.clear(); else truncate to max(0, remaining - marker_len) then push marker if remaining >= marker_len. That guarantees used+remaining ≤ limit. Do:

```rust
if text.chars().count() > remaining {
   let marker = "\n[budget global ...]";
   let marker_len = marker.chars().count();
   let keep = remaining.saturating_sub(marker_len);
   text = text.chars().take(keep).collect();
   if remaining >= marker_len { text.push_str(marker); }
}
```
Then used += len ≤ remaining. Fix.

