In `after_completed` and `reconcile`, `fail` takes ownership of RunState but we have `&mut`. Add a `fail_in_place` helper that takes `&mut RunState` and returns `Result<Step, AgentError>` (always Step::Stop). Simpler: add

```rust
async fn fail_here(
    &self,
    state: &mut RunState,
    code: impl Into<String>,
    message: impl Into<String>,
    retryable: bool,
    sink: &mut dyn EventSink,
) -> Result<Step, AgentError> {
    let code = code.into();
    let message = message.into();
    state.status = RunStatus::Failed;
    state.touch();
    self.store.save(state).await?;
    sink.emit(AgentEvent::Failed { code, message, retryable });
    Ok(Step::Stop)
}
```

