Now patch fetch script. Let me rewrite the whole file to be clean (~140 lines), under limit.

New script:
```js
// ...
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
...
const PINNED_VERSION = "2026.11.0";
...
const version = process.env.CLOUDFLARED_VERSION?.trim() || PINNED_VERSION;
...
function sha256(buf){...}
function expectedHash(asset){ read join(root,"scripts","cloudflared.sha256"); parse; }
function verify(buf, asset, label){ const exp=...; if(!exp){ console.warn...; return; } const got=...; if(got!==exp) throw... }
...
if (existsSync(dest)&&!FORCE) {
  const buf=readFileSync(dest);
  try { verify(buf,asset,"binaire existant"); console.log("déjà présent"); return; }
  catch(e){ console.error(e.message); process.exit(1); } // refuse
}
```
But existing Windows binary hash matches lowercase. Good.

If `CLOUDFLARED_VERSION` overrides, expected hash from pinned version may not match. Only verify if version === PINNED_VERSION; else warn that verification is skipped. Spec pin, but env override is dev. Implement:
```js
const pinned = version === PINNED_VERSION;
function expectedHash(asset){ if(!pinned) return null; ... }
```
If existing and !pinned, no verify. Fine.

The fallback copy from Program Files: verify hash of copied; if mismatch -> remove and fail? Do.

tgz: verify downloaded tgz.

At end write hash? no.

Also notice license already static.

Let's write.

